WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.071 --> 00:00:16.828
"Wake up!" the computer said. "This is your second wake-up call!"

2
00:00:16.829 --> 00:00:24.943
Ally sat up in bed and yawned. "It's morning already? But I just went to sleep."

3
00:00:24.944 --> 00:00:27.504
"You went dormant at one o'clock in the morning.

4
00:00:27.505 --> 00:00:32.997
You had five hours of sleep, three hours less than your standard resting period."

5
00:00:32.998 --> 00:00:35.594
"I was too worried to sleep.

6
00:00:35.595 --> 00:00:40.539
I have to figure out a way to sneak into Dr. Lloyd's office at the exhibit opening.

7
00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.778
And I have no good ideas."

8
00:00:43.779 --> 00:00:49.993
The computer whirred. "According to my analysis, the gallery has perfect acoustics when it's empty.

9
00:00:49.994 --> 00:00:54.258
Advice: create a diversion to distract Dr. Lloyd."

10
00:00:54.259 --> 00:00:58.473
"What do perfect acoustics have to do with anything?" Ally asked.

11
00:00:58.474 --> 00:01:04.092
"You can activate your voice-throwing ability to call Dr. Lloyd away to another part of the museum." "Brilliant!

12
00:01:04.093 --> 00:01:07.701
Why didn't I think of that?" Alpha's

13
00:01:07.702 --> 00:01:13.091
lights blinked. "You do not possess my superior computing powers." "True."

14
00:01:13.092 --> 00:01:17.786
Ally jumped up and did a quick dance move. "And

15
00:01:17.787 --> 00:01:31.202
you do not possess my superior dance powers!" ***

16
00:01:31.203 --> 00:01:36.585
"Morning, Ally!" Mateo said when Ally got to work. He was sitting at the counter with Phil.

17
00:01:36.586 --> 00:01:41.434
"Hi, Mateo," Ally said. "Phil, you're here early today."

18
00:01:41.435 --> 00:01:47.728
"The next few days are going to be very busy at the museum with the sci-fi convention," Phil replied.

19
00:01:47.729 --> 00:01:50.543
"So I'm going golfing today."

20
00:01:50.544 --> 00:01:53.392
"Where's golfing?" Ally asked.

21
00:01:53.393 --> 00:02:01.622
Mateo laughed. "Are you still half asleep, Ally? Phil is going to play golf."

22
00:02:01.623 --> 00:02:09.164
"Oh, right!" Ally faked a laugh. "Silly me!"

23
00:02:09.165 --> 00:02:13.586
"Golfing is relaxing and makes me happy," Phil said.

24
00:02:13.587 --> 00:02:21.439
"Hmm," Ally thought. Would golfing make Ray happier too?

25
00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:26.864
Ally found Ray in his office. "Did you know Phil is going golfing today?"

26
00:02:26.865 --> 00:02:27.846
"Yep."

27
00:02:27.847 --> 00:02:31.002
"Why don't you go with him," she suggested.

28
00:02:31.003 --> 00:02:32.885
"I can't leave the diner."

29
00:02:32.886 --> 00:02:39.456
"Sure you can. Randy can cook. You haven't taken any time off since we reopened."

30
00:02:39.457 --> 00:02:45.571
Ray gazed at her.

31
00:02:45.572 --> 00:02:47.862
"Maybe I could take a few hours."

32
00:02:47.863 --> 00:02:54.179
Ally nodded. "Go have fun. It'll make you happy!"

33
00:02:54.180 --> 00:03:00.497
*** After the men left, Mateo called Ally

34
00:03:00.498 --> 00:03:04.393
over. "Thank you for encouraging Papi to take time

35
00:03:04.394 --> 00:03:07.927
off. Ever since my mom left, he's had trouble

36
00:03:07.928 --> 00:03:11.036
relaxing. He worries about the diner and me too

37
00:03:11.037 --> 00:03:16.834
much." "So that's why Ray is lonely!" Ally thought. "His wife

38
00:03:16.835 --> 00:03:20.891
left." "Is that your mom in the photo on his desk?" she asked.

39
00:03:20.892 --> 00:03:22.851
Mateo nodded.

40
00:03:22.852 --> 00:03:26.471
"Has Ray ever tried to meet someone new?"

41
00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:31.067
Mateo shrugged. "He says he's too old to date."

42
00:03:31.068 --> 00:03:36.133
"Who's too old to date?" Kate asked, entering the diner.

43
00:03:36.134 --> 00:03:39.791
After Ally explained, Kate shook her head.

44
00:03:39.792 --> 00:03:43.498
"You're never too old to find love," she said.

45
00:03:43.499 --> 00:03:49.693
"That's what my aunt says. She's single, and she's about Ray's age."

46
00:03:49.694 --> 00:03:53.782
"Maybe they could date each other!" Ally thought.

47
00:03:53.783 --> 00:04:03.606
"I've got to get to soccer camp," Mateo said. "See you tomorrow for the convention."

48
00:04:03.607 --> 00:04:08.906
Ally waited for Mateo to leave before whispering her great idea to Kate.

49
00:04:08.907 --> 00:04:11.776
"Yes, let's do it!" Kate squealed.

50
00:04:11.777 --> 00:04:14.401
"I'll tell my aunt and you tell Ray.

51
00:04:14.402 --> 00:04:18.652
We can arrange to have them meet here tomorrow before we go to the convention."

52
00:04:18.653 --> 00:04:23.533
"Awesome!" Ally was excited that she'd found another way to make Ray happy.

53
00:04:23.534 --> 00:04:27.846
"Do you still want to go shopping today after your shift?" Kate asked.

54
00:04:27.847 --> 00:04:35.483
"Yes! Shopping and matchmaking sounds like the perfect day to me!"

55
00:04:35.484 --> 00:04:45.344
*** Later that afternoon, as Ally and Kate walked downtown, Ally noticed something very strange: there were alien creatures

56
00:04:45.345 --> 00:04:49.509
everywhere! She glanced at Kate, but the other girl didn't seem to notice a

57
00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:54.252
thing. "Maybe my imagination is playing tricks on me," Ally

58
00:04:54.253 --> 00:04:59.931
thought. She blinked a few times, but the aliens were still

59
00:04:59.932 --> 00:05:03.730
there. "Um, Kate, why are there so many aliens

60
00:05:03.731 --> 00:05:11.336
around?" Kate laughed. "I wish Sandville was known for something more interesting than the UFO

61
00:05:11.337 --> 00:05:18.006
museum. But I do like the sci-fi convention. It's fun, and everybody dresses up in crazy costumes."

62
00:05:18.007 --> 00:05:22.468
"Oh!" Ally laughed. "They're costumes!"

63
00:05:22.469 --> 00:05:29.497
Kate gave her an odd look. "What did you think they were? Which reminds me, we need costumes too."

64
00:05:29.498 --> 00:05:31.702
"Why?" Ally asked.

65
00:05:31.703 --> 00:05:40.864
"If we don't wear them to the convention, we'll never hear the end of it from Mateo and Bethany.

66
00:05:40.865 --> 00:05:46.250
Let's go into that store across the street," Kate suggested. "They have fun stuff."

67
00:05:46.251 --> 00:05:51.508
Ally started to follow Kate across the street. But just then she spotted a huge billboard:

68
00:05:51.509 --> 00:05:58.487
"The Sandville Sci-Fi Convention Presents Dr. Cosmo Lloyd and a Special Out-of-This-World Guest!"

69
00:05:58.488 --> 00:06:05.219
Beside the words, for the entire town to see, was a silhouette of . . . an Astralian!

70
00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:11.938
Ally gasped. "Is that me?"

